# =============================================================================
# Node Attribution Resolver — Configuration
# =============================================================================
#
# This file is the single source of the resolver's configurable values.
# Wire it into the systemd service via EnvironmentFile=.
#
# Credentials are NOT configured here. The resolver uses the host instance's
# IAM role (boto3 default credential chain). Do NOT add static keys.
#
# This component is OPTIONAL — only needed if you want to resolve client IPs
# to their EC2 instance Name tags. Without it, the collector still works fine
# and reports raw IPs.

# --- AWS Region ---
# The AWS region the EC2 describe APIs are targeted at. Leave BLANK to
# auto-detect from IMDS (recommended — works in any region automatically).
# Set explicitly only to force a specific region.
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1

# --- Attribution Refresh Interval ---
# How often the cache is refreshed. Default: 5m. This is deliberately slower
# than the collector's 60s cadence to avoid EC2 API throttling.
ATTRIBUTION_REFRESH_INTERVAL=5m

# --- Cache file path ---
# Where the resolver writes the Client_IP -> {name_tag, instance_id} cache.
# Must match CLIENT_NODE_CACHE in config/collector.env.
CLIENT_NODE_CACHE=/usr/local/percona/pmm/collectors/textfile-collector/.client_node_cache.tsv

# --- Optional: scope the ENI lookup to a single VPC ---
# Leave blank to enumerate all ENIs in the region. Set to a VPC id to filter.
# NODE_ATTRIBUTION_VPC_ID=vpc-0123456789abcdef0
